- ## Notes
- - **Reuse API Keys**: No new auth profiles needed. Existing keys (`kimi-coding:default`, `anthropic:default`, etc.) are automatically shared across all agents.
- - **Workspace location**: All agent workspaces go in `/root/.openclaw/workspace-groups/{agentname}/`
- - **One channel is enough**: Agent is live as soon as one channel is connected.
- - **Multiple channels**: Add multiple account entries and bindings to connect one agent to multiple channels.
- ## Common Mistakes
- | ❌ Wrong | ✅ Correct |
- |---------|----------|
- | `binding.match.account` | `binding.match.accountId` |
- | `botToken` at top level (Telegram) | `accounts.{name}.botToken` |
- | `agents.list[].telegramAccount` | Use `bindings` for routing |
- | `routing` field | Use `bindings` |
